        "readability": 6.5,
        "reasons": {
          "overallMobile": "Two complete mission loops with understandable objectives, strong atmosphere and workable assisted touch controls; crowded HUD and reliance on contextual guidance limit confidence in free manual play.",
          "controls": "Native two-contact MOVE and FIRE drag produced visible patrol eliminations in each attempt; scene swipe worked. Tap aim assistance was effective. Short interrupted contacts cannot grade sustained rearming or thumb comfort.",
          "gameplay": "Recovery, coil disabling and deck upload gave a clear sequence and visible progress; most traversal was route assisted, limiting assessment of navigation and combat depth. Stationary upload succeeded with remaining shield; this alone does not establish balance or enjoyment.",
          "presentation": "Cohesive rainy industrial setting, cyan/amber color language, weapon and result screen gave a consistent atmosphere. Audio and hardware rendering unassessed.",
          "usability": "Large primary touch buttons, changing hold labels, map legend/route length and explicit assist counters were useful. Coil I required repositioning after a generic MAP cue; the map helped once.",
          "readability": "Health, ammo and terminal stats readable; distant patrol silhouettes and small environmental labels were harder at 844x390. Large right-side threat banners consume scene area."
        }
      },
